# NEXORA release handoff

NEXORA is a server-enforced AI security and governance control plane for model
traffic, agents and MCP tools.

Live release: https://nexora-guard-core.lovable.app
Repository: https://github.com/adreinmorin-design/nexora-guard-core-695d0312

## Start here

1. Open the live URL and create an operator account.
2. Configure at least one provider secret in the deployment environment.
3. Open **AI Gateway → Providers** and confirm `CONFIGURED`.
4. Run a non-sensitive request in **Gateway → Playground**.
5. Review **Plans & Billing**, **Agents**, **Security** and **AI Efficiency**.

## Provider setup

Native adapters support OpenAI, Anthropic and Google Gemini. Any vendor or
private gateway using the OpenAI Chat Completions shape can be added with
`NEXORA_<VENDOR>_API_KEY` and `NEXORA_<VENDOR>_BASE_URL`. Provider keys never
reach browser code.

## Paddle setup

Paddle checkout is implemented but stays disabled until the Paddle client token,
checkout-signing secret, webhook secret, and Solo/Team price IDs are supplied.
Register `/api/paddle/webhook` as the notification destination. Entitlements
change only after a verified webhook.

## Efficiency playbook

Use **AI Efficiency Playbook** to inventory calls, route simple work to cheaper
models, reuse structured prompts, retrieve only needed evidence, scope agents
as identities, and measure cost per business outcome. Start with a 30-day
baseline before expanding automation.

## Verification

```bash
npm install
npm run lint
npm run test:gateway
npm run test:security
npm run test:agents
npm run test:providers
npm run test:paddle
npm run test:billing
npm run test:database
npx tsc --noEmit
npm run build
```

GitHub Actions uses `npm install --ignore-scripts` because this Lovable checkout
does not yet contain a lockfile. Add and commit a lockfile before making CI
reproducibility a release gate.
